Flag parent-element mismatch as type conflict

When two ConcreteTypes with the same TypeId get assigned to the same
equivalence class but their parent elements live in distinct classes,
Structure::close used to enqueue pairwise parent equalities, silently
collapsing the parents. This is wrong for the multi-model setting:
distinct ambient parents should not be unified by an inferred type.
Now drain_equalities and impose_concrete_type record a TypeConflict
in that case, leaving the parents untouched. TypeConflict's docstring
notes that types may carry the same TypeId twice.
